t."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In front of a full stadium of 75,000 fans, Duplantis then asked for 6.25 metres, one centimetre above his world record. He needed three attempts but he got over it on his final effort for another world record. It was only the second world record in the pole vault at the Olympics, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/74763"} "Władysław Kozakiewicz"] " jumped 5.78 m to win the Moskva 1980 gold medal. Duplantis became the second athlete to win two Olympic pole vault gold medals, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/78946"} "Bob Richards"] " (USA) in 1952-56."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1233"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/146747"} "Mondo Duplantis"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "5.75 (=1)"] [:td {} "6.25 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1318"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/136266"} "Sam Kendricks"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "5.75 (8)"] [:td {} "5.95 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "790"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143515"} "Emmanouil Karalis"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GRE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GRE.png"}] "GRE"]] [:td {} "5.75 (=1)"] [:td {} "5.90 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]]